  "path": "backlog/tasks/task-7.32 - Investigate-why-advised-play-almost-never-folds-after-the-flop-WTSD-~94.md",
  "description": "Found while specifying TASK-10.3: in 100,000-hand 6-max playtests (seeds 42 and 7) the all-TAG line-up shows WTSD 94.4%/94.3% (VPIP 22.2, PFR 16.2, Aggression 63, W$SD 50). TAG bots fold after the flop in only ~3.4% of flops seen (98 folds in 2,855 seat-hands), and every bot style in the Mixed line-up sits at 92-96% WTSD. Healthy limit play folds far more postflop (realistic WTSD roughly 30-42% at 6-max). Bots and the user's hints share the postflop advice, so the trainer may be teaching over-calling. Find the cause (pot-odds thresholds, range model, equity vs opponent ranges, bot style policies) and fix it, then re-run TASK-10.3's WTSD check.",
  "dependencies": [
    "TASK-10.3"
